    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-0",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring Boot test support"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-0-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "spring-boot-starter-test",
          [
            [
              "c"
            ]
          ]
        ],
        [
          " supplies Boot-managed test libraries. These include JUnit Jupiter, Mockito, AssertJ, and Spring test support."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-0-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "JUnit Jupiter runs test methods. Mockito supplies controlled stand-ins for dependencies. AssertJ supplies assertions."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-0-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Spring test support can create an application context for tests that need Spring beans."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-0-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A plain Java test does not need a Spring context. It can call a constructor directly."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-1",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Test scope"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-1-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The test annotation determines how much Spring configuration is loaded."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-1-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A slice test loads one selected part of the application, such as Spring MVC."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-1-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A full application-context test loads the application configuration and its beans."
        ]
      ]
    },
