        [
          "Test dependency"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-2-example-0",
      "type": "example",
      "example": {
        "title": "Add the managed test starter",
        "language": "text",
        "description": [
          "Java `17` and Maven are required. The files form a separate project rooted at `pom.xml`.",
          "`TitlePolicyTest` uses the managed test starter to check `TitlePolicy`."
        ],
        "code": "",
        "explanation": [
          "`test` makes these libraries available to test compilation and execution.",
          "Production classes remain in `src/main/java`. Test classes belong in `src/test/java`.",
          "Boot dependency management selects compatible library versions.",
          "The next lessons explain JUnit annotations, repeated inputs, Mockito dependencies, the MVC slice, and the full application context in that order."
        ],
        "commands": "mvn test",
        "files": [
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/DemoApplication.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\n\nimport org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;\nimport org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;\n\n@SpringBootApplication\npublic class DemoApplication {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        SpringApplication.run(DemoApplication.class, args);\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/main/java/com/example/demo/TitlePolicy.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\npublic class TitlePolicy {\n    public String normalize(String title) { return title.strip(); }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "src/test/java/com/example/demo/TitlePolicyTest.java",
            "language": "java",
            "code": "package com.example.demo;\nimport org.junit.jupiter.api.Test;\nimport static org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions.assertEquals;\nclass TitlePolicyTest {\n    @Test\n    void removesOuterWhitespace() {\n        assertEquals(\"First entry\", new TitlePolicy().normalize(\"  First entry  \"));\n    }\n}\n"
          },
          {
            "name": "pom.xml",
            "language": "text",
            "code": "<project xmlns=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0\" xmlns:xsi=\"http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance\"\n         xsi:schemaLocation=\"http://maven.apache.org/POM/4.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/maven-4.0.0.xsd\">\n    <modelVersion>4.0.0</modelVersion>\n    <parent>\n        <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n        <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-parent</artifactId>\n        <version>3.5.16</version>\n        <relativePath/>\n    </parent>\n    <groupId>com.example</groupId>\n    <artifactId>demo</artifactId>\n    <version>1.0.0</version>\n    <properties><java.version>17</java.version></properties>\n    <dependencies>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-web</artifactId>\n        </dependency>\n        <dependency>\n            <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n            <artifactId>spring-boot-starter-test</artifactId>\n            <scope>test</scope>\n        </dependency>\n    </dependencies>\n    <build>\n        <finalName>demo</finalName>\n        <plugins>\n            <plugin>\n                <groupId>org.springframework.boot</groupId>\n                <artifactId>spring-boot-maven-plugin</artifactId>\n            </plugin>\n        </plugins>\n    </build>\n\n</project>\n"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-3",
      "type": "header",
      "richText": [
        [
          "What each scope proves"
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-3-note-0",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A mock can return a configured value. It does not prove that the real database or remote API works."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-3-note-1",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "A test that only starts the context checks startup. Assertions are still needed to check application behavior."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-3-note-2",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "Tests that load real data connections need isolated test configuration and data."
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "test-framework-lesson-3-note-3",
      "type": "bulleted_list",
      "richText": [
        [
          "The MVC lesson explains mock HTTP requests. The application-test lesson explains real-server requests and transaction boundaries."
        ]
      ]
    }
  ],
